# EKF3 optical flow fusion — Stage A of the EKF baseline (see CLAUDE.md,
# "Downward Optical Flow — EKF3 Fusion (Stage A)"). Injected via MAVLink
# OPTICAL_FLOW by flow_bridge.py.
#
# Stage A proves flow velocity fusion only - GPS stays as the POSXY source
# (EK3_SRC1_POSXY is deliberately left untouched, GPS/3, not set here).
# This is NOT a GNSS-denied navigation config; that is a separate later step.
#
# FLOW_TYPE=5 (MAVLink) selects the AP_OpticalFlow_MAV backend, which reads
# OPTICAL_FLOW's flow_rate_x/flow_rate_y extension fields.
FLOW_TYPE 5
# EK3_SRC1_VELXY=5 (OpticalFlow) - required by NavEKF3_core::readyToUseOptFlow().
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 5
# EK3_FLOW_USE=1 (Navigation) - already the Copter default, set explicitly
# because readyToUseOptFlow() hard-fails if this is 2 (Terrain-only).
EK3_FLOW_USE 1
# Camera body-frame position offset (FRD, +Z down). Camera is at z=-0.25 m in
# the SDF; LiDAR at z=-0.12 m; base_link = IMU/body origin (imu_link 0 0 0).
# On centreline, X=Y=0.
#
# 0.13 is NOT a physical measurement of where the camera sits (that would be
# 0.25, camera-from-origin). It is the camera-to-RANGEFINDER offset
# (0.25 - 0.12), set so that EKF3's optical-flow model receives the correct
# camera height GIVEN that RNGFND1_POS_Z cancels out of that path.
#
# Source trace: the flow terrain height is heightAboveGnd = terrainState - pd
# with terrainState = rng*c.z + pd (AP_NavEKF3_OptFlowFusion.cpp:112,:298), so
# pd (origin height) CANCELS and the flow height baseline is the RAW
# rangefinder reading, which is LiDAR-referenced - readRangeFinder
# (AP_NavEKF3_Measurements.cpp:85-88) stores the raw distance and never applies
# RNGFND1_POS_Z. Line :317 then subtracts FLOW_POS_Z from that LiDAR-referenced
# range, so EKF3 computes camera_height ~= lidar_range - FLOW_POS_Z. The value
# that yields the true camera height is therefore the camera-to-LiDAR
# separation 0.13, not the literal camera-from-origin 0.25 (which would
# over-correct to 1.90 m, -5.9%). The validation trial's empirical residual is
# the arbiter (pre-registered: |residual| <= 2% accept). See CLAUDE.md.
FLOW_POS_X 0
FLOW_POS_Y 0
FLOW_POS_Z 0.13
